T1  - A randomised control trial comparing the efficacy of LMA-supreme and I-gel as rescue ventilatory device in patients with simulated difficult airway undergoing anaesthesia with controlled ventilation
A1  - Rahman S.
A1  - Agarwal N.
A1  - Guria S.
A1  - Jain S.
A1  - Swain M.
Y1  - 2021//
N2  - Introduction: In an unanticipated difficult airway or in an emergency situation of cannot-intubate-cannot-ventilate scenario, Supraglottic Airway Devices (SGD) are recommended as rescue devices for establishing airway quickly to prevent hypoxia. Aim(s): To compare efficacy of i-gel airway and Laryngeal Mask Airway supreme (LMA supreme) as ventilatory devices and the time taken for their insertion in anaesthetised and paralysed patients with simulated difficult airway. Material(s) and Method(s): One hundred and eighty adult patients with simulated difficult airway were randomly allocated to two groups of 90 patients each. In group I: i-gel and in group S: LMA supreme was inserted. Primary outcome studied was time taken for insertion of SGD. Secondary outcomes were the number of attempts taken for insertion of device, oropharyngeal leak pressure, ease of gastric catheter insertion, fibreoptic bronchoscopic view of anatomical alignment of device with glottic opening. Quantitative variables were compared usin unpaired t-test/Mann-Whitney Test, between the two group Qualitative variable were compared using Chi-Square tes Fisher's-exact test. Result(s): Total time taken for successful insertion wa significantly shorter with group i-gel as compared to grou LMA supreme {median (IQR) {19(18.25-21)} versus{24 (2 24)} with p-value<=0.0001. Overall success rate of insertio (96.67% vs 97.78%, p=1.000) and oropharyngeal leak pressu (p-value=0.555) of i-gel and LMA-S were comparable. i-gel ha better anatomic alignment with glottic opening as compared t LMA-S (p-value <=0.0001). Gastric tube insertion was easy in patients in both the groups. Conclusion(s): Shorter time for the insertion of i-gel wa observed due to absence of inflatable cuff, although bot LMA-S and i-gel are equally efficacious as ventilatory device in patients with simulated difficult airway under general anaesthesia with controlled ventilation.Copyright © 2021 Journal of Clinical and Diagnostic Research. All rights reserved.
