N2  - The proceedings contain 204 papers. The topics discussed include: gluten-free option and vegan version for micro-vessel manufacture for vascular access training; paediatric deaths and the paediatric intensive care unit registrar: grief reactions, coping strategies and supports utilised; the embalming army technique: regional anaesthesia specimens made easy; observational study of the effect of tracheal intubation and tracheal tube position on regional lung ventilation during general anaesthesia; cardiopulmonary exercise testing to detect patients with exercise-induced myocardial ischaemia and unidentified increased mortality in major oncological colorectal surgery; evaluation of accuracy of non-invasive haemoglobin estimation by pulse oximetry during major surgical haemorrhage; light at the end of the tunnel for high-fidelity airway training; low-dose S+ ketamine in target-controlled intravenous anaesthesia with remifentanil and propofol for open gynaecological surgery: a randomised controlled trial; pilot of the research and audit federation of trainees national project 3: drug allergy labels in elective surgical patients (DALES): innovative data collection and study set-up techniques; comparison of a novel point-of-care coagulation testing device (QuantraTM) with thromboelastography and laboratory testing; and spinal anaesthesia for emergency caesarean section in severe factor 12 deficiency.
