N2  - The proceedings contain 193 papers. The special focus in this conference is on Cardiothoracic Anaesthesiologists. The topics include: current technological and non-technological trends in cardiovascular fields; wireless anaesthetic data management; biomarkers in preoperative risk assessment and optimization in vascular surgery; neurological monitoring during vascular sugery; indication, contraindication and controversies for endovascular aortic replacement in Abdominal Aortic Aneurysm and thoracoabdominal aneurysm; management of ruptured abdominal aortic aneurysms; anaesthetic and postoperative management in Endovascular Aortic replacement; delirium after cardiac surgery; the bleeding patient; impact of the age of red blood cells and the outcome after cardiac surgery; new oral anticoagulants in cardiac surgery - management of coagulation and haemostasis; alternatives to heparin during cardiopulmonary bypass and in the intensive care unit; only cardiothoracic anaesthetists can be good cardiothoracic intensivists; pharmacoeconomics of transfusion; an evidence-based approach to support the routine use of ultrasound for vascular access; goal directed monitoring in cardiothoracic and vascular intensive care; restricted therapy is best; pro position; lung recriutment in thoracic surgery. con position; left-sided DLTs for everyone; right-sided DLTs for left pulmonary resections; optimalisation of ventilation using a new impedance tomography monitor; usefulness of extracorporeal support systems during thoracic surgery; volumetric capnography for monitoring and predicting the effect of PEEP on oxygenation during one-lung ventilation; perioperative renal protection strategies in cardiac surgery; basic mechanisms of acute lung injury; perioperative lung injuries; the effects of steroids on cerebral outcomes after cardiac surgery; EACTA thoracic subcommittee European survey on "One lung intubation"; prompt brain death diagnosis in the potential donor. implications for cardiothoracic organ function; optimal ventilation in postoperative lung transplant; twenty years' leap in perfusion education in Europe; experience in multidisciplinary simulation training in perfusion incidents; coagulation and anticoagulation in paediatric cardiac patients; ethical issues around research in paediatric cardiac surgery; mediastinal mass in the pregnant patient; tracheal dehiscence - management; the patient with severe heart disease requiring OLV for non cardiac surgery; acute renal failure in paediatric cardiac surgery; recent developments; anaesthetic management and outcomes of hybrid procedures at the cardiovascular institute of the Fuwai hospital; anaesthetic management of adult congenital heart disease; perioperative pain therapy; effect of depth of anaesthesia and cerebral oxygenation on postoperative cognitive function in patients undergoing cardiac surgery; peripheral tissue oxygen saturation during cardiac surgery and postoperative outcome; incidence, causes and outcome of emergency cardiac surgery and emergency cardiopulmonary bypass in 994 patients for transcatheter aortic valve implantation (TAVI); postoperative bleeding after cardiac surgery is associated with increased need for organ support and higher 30-day mortality; assessment of myocardial damage among vascular and thoracic surgery patients by late enhancement cardiac magnetic resonance imaging after postoperative troponin elevation; cardiac complications following lower limb arterial bypass surgery in West of Scotland; haemodynamic and cerebral oxygenation changes during carotid endarterectomy under local anaesthesia; transcatheter aortic valve replacement (TAVI) in patients aged 90 years or more; incidence and outcome of atrioventricular block after transcatheter aortic valve implantation (TAVI); copeptin as a marker for stress in surgical (SAVR) and transcatheter aortic valve replacement (TAVI); sevoflurane optimal dosage for myocardium pharmacological postconditioning; association of perioperative troponin and atrial fibrillation after coronary artery bypass grafting; intraoperative intraaortic balloon pump versus levosimendan in high risk cardiac patients; relationship between cardiac output, bispectral index and cerebral oxygen saturations in cardiac surgery; early extubation after cardiac surgery is associated with better postoperative cognitive function; haemodynamic changes after single dose remifentanil or sufentanil; a randomised study in cardiac surgery patients; single bolus of propofol in patients with brugada syndrome; advantages of on-pump beating-heart CABG in patients with a low ejection fraction; effects of the cardiac output on sevoflurane pharmacodynamics; effects of remote ischaemic preconditioning on oxidative stress in cardiac surgery; effects of the remote ischaemic preconditioning on the myocardial injury in the patients undergoing aortic valve replacement; the influence of inotropic drugs on the outcome of the GLUTAMICS trial; patients with continued antiplatelet therapy before coronary artery bypass grafting; ticagrelor and acute cardiac surgery; postoperative bleeding associated with change in heparin supplier; diagnosis, perioperative monitoring, and treatment of patients with pulmonary hypertension and/or right ventricular dysfunction in Germany; effect of oral sildenafil on perioperative pulmonary hypertension in patients undergoing mitral valve replacement surgery; effect of cardiopulmonary bypass (CPB) and deep hypothermic circulatory arrest (DHCA) on propofol pharmaco kinetics; single dose aminoglycoside has an impact on renal function but does not increase postoperative dialysis after cardiac surgery; pharmacokinetics of cefetaxime in ICU-patients treated with continuous renal replacement; mediastinitis after cardiac surgery; systemic inflammatory response syndrome after surgery for triple valve disease; influence of the remote ischemic preconditioning on the inflammatory response in patients undergoing aortic valve replacement; prediction of fluid responsiveness and relationship with clinical outcomes in CABG; echocardiographic study of right ventricular systolic function after aortic valve replacement for stenosis; in vivo effects of volatile anaesthetics and positive pressure ventilation on left atrial dimensions and function in healthy adults; anaesthetic management for off-pump implantation of left ventricular assist device; levosimendan infusion during ECMO weaning; fungal ventricular assist device (VAD) infections occur in colonised patients and are associated with high mortality rate; predictive factors of survival in patients treated with polymyxin-B haemoperfusion for endotoxic shock following cardiac surgery; combined high central venous oxygen saturation and blood lactate levels and outcome in cardiac surgery patients; cerebral saturation response to pre-oxygenation and induction of anaesthesia and cerebral desaturation during one-lung ventilation; precision and construct validity of extravascular lung water measurement following lung resection; comparison of the performance of standard double lumen tubes with vivasight-DLTM double lumen tubes for lung isolation during thoracic surgery; high thoracic epidural analgesia supplement may protect renal function in cardiac surgery patients; preoperative renal function and risk identification in cardiac surgery; on-pump CABG is associated with more renal desaturation and higher biomarker values for acute kidney injury than off-pump CABG; the influence of serum neutrophil gelatinase associated lipocalin levels on early detection of acute kidney injury in patients with insulin dependent diabetes mellitus undergoing cardiac surgery; feasibility of contrast echocardiograpy in assessment of total aortic regurgitation following TAVI; aetiology of preoperative anaemia in patients undergoing cardiac surgery; the influence of dexamethasone on intraoperative and postoperative lactate levels and glycaemic control in cardiac surgery patients; association between platelet count and platelet function in paediatric cardiac surgery; effect of increasing flow rate on cerebral oxygen saturation and transcranial Doppler flow velocity; prone position ventilation in cardiac surgery patients with ALI/ARDS; effect of body mass index on morbidity and stratified mortality after cardiac surgery; a comparison of the effects of midazolam and sevoflurane on myocardial protection during arterial switch operation; impact of the insulin and glucose content of postoperative fluid on the outcome after pediatric cardiac surgery; fluid overload and adverse outcomes following paediatric cardiac surgery; hypothermic versus normothermic cardiopulmonary bypass in patients with valvular heart disease; optimisation of both macro and microcirculation with low dose noradrenaline confirmed by microvision imaging; on-pump CABG safety assessment using the artificial neural networks; myocardial sevoflurane postconditioning during cardiac operation with prolonged aorta cross-clamp period; putative biomarkers of acute kidney injury are related to the duration of cardiopulmonary bypass; blood lactate level and venous oximetry in cardiac surgery patients; patient experience end satisfaction with cardiac anaesthesia; management and outcome of out-of-hospital cardiac arrest; milrinone relaxes pulmonary veins in precision-cut lung slices from guinea pigs and humans; a meta-analysis of randomised controlled trials on dexmedetomidine in critically ill patients; simple method to prevent microcirculation disturbances; a comparison of interindividual variability between thromboelastography (TEG) and rotational thromboelastometry (ROTEM); tricuspid annular plane systolic excursion (TAPSE) in the modified deep trangastric right ventricle view as an alternative for right ventricular function assessment; esmolol as a treatment of refractory hypoxaemia during veno-venous ECMO; direct complications of "Avalon" cannula use for adult respiratory ECMO; need for vasoconstrictors after cardiac surgery in patients with reduced preoperative left ventricular function; relation between organ dysfunction and 30-day mortality after cardiac surgery; the efficacy of extubation in operating room flowing TCPC procedure in paediatric patients; respiratory change in blood flow profile at the site of anastomosis after bidirectional Glenn operation; relationship between serum concentration of tranexamic acid and blood loss in paediatric cardiac surgery; lung transplantation for pulmonary fibrosis; acute mesenteric ischaemia after cardiopulmonary bypass; the association of lowest haematocrit and intra-operative transfusion during cardiopul-monary bypass with acute kidney injury; fondaparinux management for heparin-induced thrombocytopenia in postoperative cardiac surgery patients; a meta-analysis of randomised trials on percutaneous tracheostomy techniques in critically ill adults; mortality in high risk septic patients treated with drotrecogin ALFA or placebo; lower levels of glycosylated haemoglobin can assess increased postoperative renal complication risk in coronary bypass patients; impact of the preceding time of coronary angiography on acute kidney injury after elective off-pump coronary artery bypass surgery; association of the ACE D allele with acute kidney injury in non-Chinese patients after cardiac surgery; furosemide bolus in acute kidney injury; fast track cardiac anaesthesia decreases ICU length of stay without compromising outcome; comparison between the effects of retrograde and antegrade cold-blood cardioplegia on right ventricular function assessed by transoesophageal echocardiography; the effect of pre-operative betablocker treatment in cardiac surgery patients with or without COPD on postoperative extubation time and ICU length of stay; a Bayesian network meta-analysis of randomised trials on anaesthetic drugs and survival in cardiac surgery; anaesthetic management for off-pump implantation of partial mechanical support systems; extracorporeal life support; robotic assisted mitral valve surgery experiences; left ventricular outflow tract obstruction after cardiopulmonary bypass; clinical evaluation of an endotracheal impedance cardiography cardiac output monitoring method versus continuous termodilution; haemodynamic effects of low versus moderate dose opioid anaethesia; the effect of milrinone on mortality in cardiac surgery; impact of intra-aortic balloon pump on cerebral oxygenation in patients undergoing CABG; transcatheter aortic valve implantation; incidence and perioperative risk factors of acute kidney injury after oesophageal surgery for cancer; randomised control trial comparing the glidescope and macintosh laryngoscope for double lumen endotracheal tube intubation; pressure and volume controlled ventilation during OLV; paravertebral levobupivacaine and ropivacaine differences in pain relief after thoracotomy; evaluation of the coagulation profiles of preserved autologous whole blood using rotation tromboelastometry; ativated factor V11a increases postoperative cerebrovascular events in patients undergoing aortic surgery with deep hypothermic circulatory arrest and the effect of 6% hydroxyethyl starch and 3% modified fluid gelatin on thromboelastography parameters in patients undergoing coronary surgery.
