T1  - The ED50 of propofol for successful intubation without neuromuscular blockade in children under 3 years
T3  - International Heart Forum 2009. Beijing China.
A1  - Zhang X.L.
A1  - Wang W.P.
A1  - Xu J.H.
A2  - Hu S.
Y1  - 2009//
N2  - Objective: To investigate the ED50 of propofol alone as an induction agent for endotracheal intubation for the children less than 3 years. Method(s): We conducted a prospective, controlled trial of children under 3 years who required non-emergency endotracheal intubation in Fu Wai hospital (including ASD, VSD and PDA) Thirty-one unpremedicated ASA physical status I or II patients were anesthetized with propofol alone for induction. The ED50 of propofol for airway device placement was determined using Dixon' s up-and-down method. The concentration of propofol for consecutive patients was determined by the response of the previous patient, using increments or decrements of 0. 2 mg/kg. Intubating conditions were evaluated according to a scoring system described by Viby-Mogensen. The effective dose (ED50) of propofol enabling successful tracheal intubation was determined by calculating the midpoint concentration of all independent pairs of patients after at least seven crossover points (i. e. success to failure of tracheal intubation) were obtained. The ED50 was defined as the average of crossover midpoints in each pair. Blood pressure, heart rate, Bis and Sp02 were recorded during induction. Hemodynamic data changes were compared by repeated measures ANA0VA., and P-value <0. 05 was significant. Result(s): The bolus ED50 of propofol required for successful tracheal intubation was 4. 84 (0. 28) mg/kg. From probit analysis, ED95 of propofol 5. 84 mg/kg (95% confidence limits 5. 40-9. 72 mg/kg). With ED50 induction, MAP decreased 6. 8% (70. 1 +/- 8. 8 mmHg vs. 65. 3 +/- 8. 2 mmHg, P <0. 05), returned to baseline after intubation. No patients suffered from significant bradycardia or hypotension. Conclusion(s): The ED50 of propofol for successful intubation without neuromuscular blockade in children under 3 years e is 4. 84 mg/kg. A higher induction dose of propofol alone in children than in adults and no patients suffered clinicaly significant bradycardia or hypotension.It was safe to use higher dose of propofol alone to induct in children under 3 years.
